JamesDSP -- the CONTROL APP. Built from source, not fetched.

The APK and Android.bp here are BUILD OUTPUT and are gitignored. Produce them
with:
    bash tools/build-jamesdsp.sh

WHAT CHANGED (2026-08-25, v2 build 1)
    Until now this directory held a FETCHED APK of the ROOTLESS upstream
    (me.timschneeberger.rootlessjamesdsp), and the app that actually shipped was
    jamesdsp-app/ -- james34602's classic DSPManager, versionName 9.1. That app
    was ~7 years old in look and feel, and its notification could not be
    dismissed: HeadsetService created its channel IMPORTANCE_NONE but called
    startForeground with setOngoing(true), and Android floors FGS notifications
    to LOW regardless. Both are now replaced by the modern upstream, built from
    source in the `rootFdroid` flavor.

WHY BUILT AND NOT DOWNLOADED
    A prebuilt root-full APK does exist on the author's nightly server, and it
    is NOT shippable:
        5 x libcrashlytics*.so + a live firebase-settings.crashlytics.com endpoint
        REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES + UPDATE_PACKAGES_WITHOUT_USER_ACTION, i.e. a
          system app that can silently replace itself from a third-party server
    Building lets us pick the flavor and patch out the rest.

    ⚠ AND THE FLAVOR ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH. UpdateManager is split on the
    "version" dimension, not "dependencies", so rootFdroid removes Firebase and
    leaves the self-updater fully intact. tools/jamesdsp-patches/ stubs it and
    drops the two install permissions. See that directory's RATIONALE.md.

WHY IT IS A DROP-IN
    The rootFdroid flavor sets applicationId "james.dsp" -- the same package the
    old in-tree app produced -- and drives the SAME system audio effect, checked
    by UUID rather than assumed:
        configs/audio/audio_effects.xml      f27317f4-c984-4de6-9a90-545759495bf2
        JamesDspRemoteEngine.kt:300          f27317f4-...  (the REMOTE engine)
    So configs/audio/audio_effects.xml and the libjamesdsp effect in the device
    tree are untouched. Only the control app moved.

🔴 NOT YET PROVEN, AND IT MATTERS
    The root flavor links topjohnwu libsu and shells out to `audioserver` and
    `setprop`. That is the Magisk pattern -- the module installs the effect after
    boot, so audioserver must be restarted -- and our ROM registers the effect at
    boot, so there should be nothing to restart. That is an EXPECTATION.
    Verify on the VANILLA kernel (no root), which is what releases ship; the
    test device is rooted and would hide a hard dependency.

    Also unverified: the APK is presigned (gradle's key), not platform-signed.
    The old app was built in-tree with platform_apis. Confirm the effect still
    attaches on a real build.
